    </assignments>
    <assignments>
        <name>Set_Tier_And_Pending</name>
        <label>Set Tier and Pending</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>350</locationY>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.AF_DiscountTier__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Get_Discount_Tier.AF_TierLevel__c</elementReference>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
        <assignmentItems>
            <assignToReference>$Record.AF_DiscountApprovalStatus__c</assignToReference>
            <operator>Assign</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Pending</stringValue>
            </value>
        </assignmentItems>
    </assignments>
    <decisions>
        <name>Has_Discount</name>
        <label>Has a Discount Been Entered/Changed?</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>134</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Discount</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Discount_Present</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.AF_DiscountAmount__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>GreaterThan</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Discountable_Lines</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Discount Present</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <name>Tier_Found</name>
        <label>Tier Found?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>242</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Set_NoTierConfigured</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Matching Tier Configured</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Tier_Is_Self_Authorized</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Discount_Tier</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Discount_Tier.AF_TierLevel__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Tier_And_NotRequired</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Tier is Self-Authorized (0)</label>
        </rules>
        <rules>
            <name>Tier_Requires_Approval</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Discount_Tier</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Discount_Tier.AF_TierLevel__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>GreaterThan</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Set_Tier_And_Pending</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Tier Requires Approval (&gt;0)</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Confirmed DoA matrix, now driven entirely by AF_DiscountApprovalTier__mdt (LFRDN-337) instead of hardcoded percentages: whenever a Sales Rep enters or changes the Discount Amount, computes the discount % and looks up which tier&apos;s Min/Max Percent band it falls into, stamping both AF_DiscountTier__c (the stable number AF_AP_Quote_DiscountTiers routes on) and AF_DiscountApprovalStatus__c. Tier 0 = self-authorized (Not Required); any tier &gt;0 = Pending, escalating through the Approval Process&apos;s steps. A discount % that matches no configured tier (e.g. a gap left in the business&apos;s matrix) deliberately falls back to Pending rather than silently skipping approval - same fail-safe philosophy as AF_FL_Reservation_EvaluateApproval&apos;s missing-threshold handling. Editing the % boundaries only ever requires editing AF_DiscountApprovalTier__mdt records, never this flow or the Approval Process. Before-save, no extra DML (the new Get_Discountable_Lines lookup is a query, not DML).

LFRDN-755 (2026-09-27): Var_DiscountPercent used to divide by {!$Record.Subtotal}, which includes
the negative Trade-In Deduction line - on a quote with a big trade-in, that shrinks the denominator
and inflates the computed percentage (e.g. 16,000 / 263,300 = 6.08% instead of the correct
16,000 / 398,300 = 4.02%), which then (a) routed the discount to a more senior approver tier than
it should have, and (b) got written onto every non-trade-in line by AF_FL_Quote_DiscountApproved,
so the customer received far more discount than was actually approved (24,216.64 applied vs 16,000
approved in the reported case). Added Get_Discountable_Lines + Loop_Discountable_Lines
(var_DiscountableSubtotal), excluding Trade-In Deduction and Discount Adjustment lines - the exact
same two-category exclusion AF_FL_Quote_DiscountApproved already uses when applying the approved
percentage to lines, so the same set of lines now drives both the percentage&apos;s numerator context
and its actual application, closing the gross-vs-net mismatch. Sums UnitPrice*Quantity
(AF_Formula_LineGross), not TotalPrice - TotalPrice already has whatever Discount% is currently on
the line baked in, so summing it would silently re-derive the percentage from an already-discounted
base on any quote that had a prior discount applied (confirmed live: using TotalPrice on a quote
already discounted at the old buggy 6.08% kept recomputing 6.08% instead of the correct 4.02%, since
374,083.36 - the already-discounted total of the two priced lines - was being used as the gross
instead of the true pre-discount 398,300). Var_DiscountPercent now divides by this
line-item-summed pre-discount total instead of the native Subtotal rollup.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>AF_Formula_LineGross</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>{!Loop_Discountable_Lines.UnitPrice} * {!Loop_Discountable_Lines.Quantity}</expression>
        <scale>2</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Var_DiscountPercent</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>IF({!var_DiscountableSubtotal} = 0, 0, ({!$Record.AF_DiscountAmount__c} / {!var_DiscountableSubtotal}) * 100)</expression>
        <scale>4</scale>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Quote Set Discount Approval Status {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Quote Set Discount Approval Status</label>
    <loops>
        <name>Loop_Discountable_Lines</name>
        <label>Loop Discountable Line Items</label>
        <locationX>120</locationX>
        <locationY>162</locationY>
        <collectionReference>Get_Discountable_Lines</collectionReference>
        <iterationOrder>Asc</iterationOrder>
        <nextValueConnector>
            <targetReference>Add_Line_To_Total</targetReference>
        </nextValueConnector>
        <noMoreValuesConnector>
            <targetReference>Get_Discount_Tier</targetReference>
        </noMoreValuesConnector>
    </loops>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Discount_Tier</name>
        <label>Get Discount Tier</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>134</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>true</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Tier_Found</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>AF_MinPercent__c</field>
            <operator>LessThan</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Var_DiscountPercent</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>AF_MaxPercent__c</field>
            <operator>GreaterThanOrEqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>Var_DiscountPercent</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>AF_DiscountApprovalTier__mdt</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Discountable_Lines</name>
        <label>Get Discountable Line Items</label>
        <locationX>120</locationX>
        <locationY>134</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Loop_Discountable_Lines</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>QuoteId</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.Id</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>AF_LineItemType__c</field>
            <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Trade-In Deduction</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <filters>
            <field>AF_LineItemType__c</field>
            <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Discount Adjustment</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>false</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>QuoteLineItem</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Has_Discount</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterFormula>{!$Record.AF_DiscountAmount__c} &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; (ISNEW() || ISCHANGED({!$Record.AF_DiscountAmount__c})) &amp;&amp; NOT(ISPICKVAL({!$Record.AF_DiscountApprovalStatus__c}, &quot;Pending&quot;))</filterFormula>
        <object>Quote</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordBeforeSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
    <variables>
        <name>var_DiscountableSubtotal</name>
        <dataType>Currency</dataType>
        <isCollection>false</isCollection>
        <isInput>false</isInput>
        <isOutput>false</isOutput>
        <scale>2</scale>
        <value>
            <numberValue>0.0</numberValue>
        </value>
    </variables>
</Flow>
